description:
Design a clock signal generator that produces a start signal based on an input clock. The module counts clock cycles, changing the `startclk` output to HIGH when the count reaches 4,194,304 cycles and returning to LOW until the count reaches 8,388,608 cycles. After this range, the count resets to zero, effectively creating a signal that toggles every 4,194,304 clock cycles, serving as a periodic start signal generator in digital systems.
module top_module(input clk,output reg startclk
