description:
Design a D flip-flop with additional functionality that behaves like a toggle flip-flop. On each positive edge of the clock, it captures the input data signal `d`, while also using the inverted data signal `~d` to influence the output `q`. The output is updated based on a toggling condition derived from the XOR operations with both `j` (the captured value of `d`) and `k` (the inverted captured value). This module combines characteristics of a D flip-flop and a JK flip-flop by incorporating toggling behavior based on the current state and the inputs.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output reg q
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output reg q
);reg j, k;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    j <= d;
    k <= ~d;
    q <= j ^ q;
    q <= k ^ q;
end

endmodule

