description:
Design a pulse-width modulation (PWM) generator that produces a PWM signal based on a clock input. The output, pwm_out, is set high for one clock cycle every four cycles of the clock, with the ability to reset the output and internal counter. When reset is activated, both the PWM output and the counter are cleared, ensuring the system can start fresh. This module is useful for applications requiring variable power control, such as dimming LEDs or controlling motor speeds.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg pwm_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg pwm_out
);reg [1:0] counter = 2'b0;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (rst) begin
    pwm_out <= 0;
    counter <= 2'b0;
  end else begin
    if (counter == 2'b11) begin
      pwm_out <= 1;
      counter <= 2'b0;
    end else begin
      pwm_out <= 0;
      counter <= counter + 1;
    end
  end
end

endmodule

