description:
Design a 4-input AND gate circuit that outputs a high signal only when all four inputs (A, B, C, D) are simultaneously high. This module utilizes three AND gates to first compute the intermediate results for pairs of inputs, then combines those results to determine the final output. The output signal X is controlled by a combinational logic block that sets it to high if the final condition of all combined inputs holds true, effectively achieving the AND operation across all four inputs.
module top_module(
    input A, B, C, D,
    output reg X
);

code:
module top_module(
    input A, B, C, D,
    output reg X
);wire A_B, C_D, A_B_C_D;

    // AND gate for inputs A and B
    and gate1(A_B, A, B);

    // AND gate for inputs C and D
    and gate2(C_D, C, D);

    // AND gate for inputs A, B, C, and D
    and gate3(A_B_C_D, A_B, C_D);

    // Output X is high only when all inputs are high
    always @(*) begin
        if (A_B_C_D == 1'b1) begin
            X = 1'b1;
        end
        else begin
            X = 1'b0;
        end
    end

endmodule

