Design a circuit that processes a 32-bit input signal. When the input value is greater than or equal to 100, the output is set to the hexadecimal value 64 (decimal 100). Conversely, if the input value is less than or equal to -100, the output is set to -64, while for all other values, the output mirrors the input. This module effectively acts as a clamping mechanism, constraining the output within the range of -64 to 100.
module top_module(
    input wire [31:0] in,
    output wire [31:0] out
);

